## Collision policy

`research`, `merge`, `deslop` and the retired `omni` are generic names (Automagik ships a separate Omni product; only a byte-exact retired description makes a dir named `omni` genie's). A host may already own a
skill under any of them in one of its agent skill homes, installed by another
catalogue or by the user. `deslop` in particular is a term several personal
catalogues already use as a prefix; genie ships the bare word only, so a
directory named `deslop-writing`, `deslop-code` or `deslop-design` is a
different path and is never touched. When genie's skills.sh pass installs over such a directory, it
backs the previous contents up first and reports the replacement, restricted to
the homes it can name in advance: the known agent-home table, every directory
the previous install record proves genie wrote, and any other discovered home
that already carries a genie-owned skill directory
(`collisionBackupHomes`, `src/lib/skills-installer.ts`).

The documented gap is the first install. With no previous install record and no
genie-owned skill yet present in that home, a foreign directory in an agent home
genie cannot name in advance is reported as changed but is NOT backed up,
because nothing at that moment distinguishes it from an unrelated tree that
merely happens to be called `skills`. The home is recorded, so the next update
does back it up. A user who owns a personal `research` or `merge` skill in an
unrecognised home should copy it aside before the first genie install.


